# Design Plan, reduced to what M1's parser accepts. See `bug.json` beside this
# file for why a reduced form exists at all, and for the six fields this one
# also holds to.
#
# The designed `design-plan.json` (`crates/core-model/domain/workflow-samples/`)
# is Armada's only instantiated loop: `draft` and `present`, with
# `present`'s `request_changes` verdict routing back to `draft`. `structure:
# loop` is not in M1's carried set, so this form keeps both steps and drops
# the loop — one pass through `draft` then `present`.
#
# **`present` carries the designed `human_always`, which is now in M1's
# carried set.** That is the half of the loop this milestone can honour: the
# thing that ends a design plan is a person reading it, and they can now read
# it. What is still missing is where `request_changes` goes -- the designed
# file routes it back to `draft`, and without `structure: loop` it puts the
# Drone back on `present` instead. Re-presenting is a nearer approximation of
# a design conversation than advancing unread, which is what `auto` did.
#
# **This workflow carries no Judge, and that is a decision rather than an
# omission.** The designed `design-plan.json` carries none either. Design Plan
# is a back-and-forth the engineer ends when the design is in a good place --
# `workflowdef-fields.toml` says treating that as a config error would break
# it. The thing that ends a design plan is a person reading it, and the loop
# that carries the reading back is `structure: loop`, which M1 does not have.
#
# So this stays thin until the loop lands, and a Judge would not make it less
# thin -- it would gate a draft on a machine's opinion of a conversation.
{
  "version": 1,
  "workflow_id": "design_plan",
  "name": "design_plan",
  "structure": "linear",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "draft",
      "label": "Draft",
      "evidence_type": "document",
      "advance_gate": "auto"
    },
    {
      "id": "present",
      "label": "Present",
      "evidence_type": "document",
      "advance_gate": "human_always"
    }
  ]
}
